IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `scp-rules`

-- Submarine Cables and Pipelines Protection Act 1963 (Cth) — the encoder's
-- tests.

§ `Tests`

GIVEN d IS A `Thing damaged`, f IS A `My fault`, p IS A `Proceedings`
GIVETH A `Cable case`
`damaging` d `with` f `tried` p MEANS
    `Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, d, f, FALSE, FALSE, p, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

`pipe` MEANS `a pipeline`
`resulted` MEANS `my conduct resulted in the break or injury`
`negligent` MEANS `I was negligent as to whether my conduct would result in it`

#ASSERT `I commit an offence` (`damaging` `pipe` `with` `resulted` `tried` `on indictment`)
#ASSERT `the maximum months for` (`damaging` `pipe` `with` `resulted` `tried` `on indictment`) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the maximum units for` (`damaging` `pipe` `with` `resulted` `tried` `on indictment`) EQUALS 20
-- s 10(2)
#ASSERT `the maximum months for` (`damaging` `pipe` `with` `resulted` `tried` `summarily`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the maximum units for` (`damaging` `pipe` `with` `resulted` `tried` `summarily`) EQUALS 10
-- s 7(1A)
#ASSERT `the maximum months for` (`damaging` `a high-voltage cable` `with` `negligent` `tried` `on indictment`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the maximum units for` (`damaging` `a high-voltage cable` `with` `negligent` `tried` `on indictment`) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT NOT (`I commit an offence` (`damaging` `pipe` `with` `neither` `tried` `on indictment`))
-- s 7(1)(a): a telephone cable must be injured so as might interrupt communications.
#ASSERT NOT (`I commit an offence` (`damaging` `a telegraph or telephone cable, not so as might interrupt communications` `with` `resulted` `tried` `on indictment`))
#ASSERT `I commit an offence` (`damaging` `a telegraph or telephone cable, so as might interrupt communications` `with` `resulted` `tried` `on indictment`)
-- s 7(2)
#ASSERT NOT (`I commit an offence` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, `pipe`, `negligent`, TRUE, TRUE, `on indictment`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT `I commit an offence` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, `pipe`, `negligent`, TRUE, FALSE, `on indictment`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- a foreign ship; and s 5
#ASSERT NOT (`I commit an offence` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `pipe`, `resulted`, FALSE, FALSE, `on indictment`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`I commit an offence` (`Cable case` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, `pipe`, `resulted`, FALSE, FALSE, `on indictment`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`I commit an offence` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `pipe`, `resulted`, FALSE, FALSE, `on indictment`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
-- s 8
#ASSERT `I must bear the repair cost` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, `pipe`, `neither`, FALSE, FALSE, `on indictment`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`I must bear the repair cost` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, `pipe`, `neither`, FALSE, FALSE, `on indictment`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE))
-- s 9
#ASSERT `I am indemnified` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `pipe`, `neither`, FALSE, FALSE, `on indictment`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`I am indemnified` (`Cable case` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `pipe`, `neither`, FALSE, FALSE, `on indictment`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE))
